  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_acd1c970ec6249f5854fc444f6b659e0",
      "statement": "The @ulabase/cli package ships both a CLI binary (ulabase, also installed as ula) and a library for idempotent, file-driven configuration of Ulabase services. The library exports include REDACTED, isRedacted, fromEnv, isEnvRef, resolveEnvRefs, defaultEnv, MissingEnvError, createAdminClient, createServiceClient, isApiError, TOKEN_VAR, sessionPath, readSession, writeSession, clearSession, resolveToken, step, defineSetup, runSetup, and all associated types.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/package.json",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8ec2a68ebaccf301d938e3f0e6de072356304d16851f4f597f7f7a13b5399b2e"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/index.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8a1bc0f4a8c19eb7447cb2cc0061b45932f1a152be1b6f6aec7cb1f4d92b77d1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d98c78ed2f6942c78f31dcf987c2799a",
      "statement": "The package has two install shapes: global (npm i -g ulabase) for the ulabase command and devDependency (npm i -D @ulabase/cli) for the library imports in setup files. The two copies interoperate because Setup is plain data and fromEnv uses Symbol.for for cross-version marker identity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/README.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:1184947e801060f7e006cfb9093cc70d39480c5155c9be46818adf67274787ef"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/env.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:50ac160185438a210c5ac7eba5c6217ae45eed6aed67058505fd8956f29f2bf6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f8d34ee5783498493fd066188180b6b",
      "statement": "The fromEnv function returns a marker object (not a string) identified by Symbol.for('@ulabase/cli:fromEnv'). The marker carries a toString that prints the variable name (never a value) and a toJSON that throws to prevent accidental serialization of unresolved markers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/env.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:50ac160185438a210c5ac7eba5c6217ae45eed6aed67058505fd8956f29f2bf6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bfea476d68184bd79a1ee305fd5e88d0",
      "statement": "resolveEnvRefs walks a value tree replacing fromEnv markers with environment values, collecting every missing variable before throwing MissingEnvError so a pipeline learns all missing secrets from one run. Empty strings are treated as missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/env.ts#L108-L134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:08da24f2accab3c1934ef78b647e592fcd205d759c1befb8f833bdc5177e98ff:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c1f208c575e470992c7248435da96f2",
      "statement": "Resolution of fromEnv markers happens at serialization time inside the admin client's updateFeatureConfig and the service client's body() helper — never before, and a dry run never calls apply so markers are never resolved. The updateFeatureConfig method is deliberately async so that resolveEnvRefs throws are caught by the caller's catch handler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/admin.ts#L208-L215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b29d235b853d4bc7f1ae47f05d156a18c3a2f8b863b84f1cc209b7a16da3034:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/service.ts#L101-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44d858a694e4d0034e6f0b1d8f1f125dbfa7005225b85ae180f90531adc399cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7f69fc1d1554866ba30092f0b6566a0",
      "statement": "Session management stores a personal access token and the admin node it was verified against at ~/.config/ulabase/session.json (or under XDG_CONFIG_HOME) with mode 0600 on both directory and file. A corrupt file reads as absent rather than throwing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/session.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:cafa705e30773c6504b7fb4f3274f79daf4064494677458fe6352437b2b986cb"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17006ca23aad40aa92d982e3cc301554",
      "statement": "resolveToken implements strict precedence: ULABASE_TOKEN env var always wins over the stored session file, with no conditions attached. This prevents a CI run from silently falling back to a session left on a shared runner.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/session.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:cafa705e30773c6504b7fb4f3274f79daf4064494677458fe6352437b2b986cb"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c123e72b7c3045df9492c1098f7641b9",
      "statement": "The CLI commands are login, logout, and setup (invoked as ulabase login, ulabase logout, ulabase setup). login verifies a token against the admin node before storing it. setup loads a setup file (default ./ulabase.setup.ts), resolves credentials, and runs steps. The ulabase new command for provisioning is specified but not built.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:3d1c56f1368fd368b1d5be633cdb48e547cd34c2538e9d6469b3317289320f58"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c3b398a500f4064ab7ea1f6c94a4475",
      "statement": "The setup file is resolved from --file or the first conventional name (ulabase.setup.ts, .mts, .js, .mjs) in the working directory. It accepts a default export or named 'setup' export; a function export is called with no arguments.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/cli.ts",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:3d1c56f1368fd368b1d5be633cdb48e547cd34c2538e9d6469b3317289320f58"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67d9bb3035f2444cbf485a9f62ec589d",
      "statement": "The admin client (createAdminClient) manages its own token in a closure rather than localStorage, silences the core's stderr logging, and provides methods for feature lifecycle (featureCatalog, listFeatures, isFeatureInstalled, configSchema, getFeatureConfig, updateFeatureConfig, installFeature, uninstallFeature, enableFeature, disableFeature, initFeature, testFeature), service token minting, and a generic fetch escape hatch. Deprecated aliases for the old plugin-based names are also exported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/admin.ts#L154-L288",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff808d2612186d5151bd3804c2fb74d50108cc4d8ce33a60344662d0824ac7e7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f1e0ce23c6d848bcb0f6a460b3f055c4",
      "statement": "The service client (createServiceClient) derives from the admin client, mints a JWT lazily on first use, caches it, renews it 60 seconds before expiry, and shares one in-flight mint between concurrent callers. The token is never returned to callers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/service.ts#L42-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5bb7a92ac86d1a6e78e159632ddeb333fe0177ac19286c5f4a737dcf7a4d1223:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a5cb4e0fcac43099e21d163534c36a9",
      "statement": "Service client checks answer false on 404 and throw on anything else (including 403), because a 403 means the token cannot see the thing, not that it is absent. Document writes (permissions, users, schemas) use ?wm=upsert; collections and indexes do not need it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/http.ts#L66-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e28777794d85fcb0f601d585f0cdfb1aba7c6821403878d1450b4c87e65d13f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/service.ts#L107-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94bb5ffda8cee0314d1a5d51f73640aaba63716057c66f0fcb6e59dd23c0d4a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ab950e43d704d76b58478e211337676",
      "statement": "A step is a { name, check, apply } pair. defineSetup(name, steps) declares a setup. runSetup executes steps sequentially, halting on failure (except in dry-run mode where it runs every check). Each step receives { service, admin, srvId }.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L108-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b62760667566b84a83b27951d76a132ddf3c54c2cef51682229dca7f6e5edc7e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L132-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5d0a41acef56dbd8289842c75c7fbaa672daadcedf85b7922be139b94897b7c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L19-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:060b8f159f5e664401af46b4408f3dfd7e875fb0bb490990ddd62c35b62130db:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_681794ceeec64c3fb2a2d89d2bb7e693",
      "statement": "The runner re-checks after applying with exponential backoff (delays of 0, 300ms, 700ms, 2s, 4s, 8s — up to ~15 seconds). This handles the lag between admin-node writes and service-node cache visibility, without turning a wrong step into a passing one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L155-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68c2c0559fce01323f31ca3e1f68f9455169209a3709573d4ca32f8bb558f517:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9966a31ac53641f18971c5f8d3796fd6",
      "statement": "The --force option skips the check but not the recheck verification. It accepts step names matched by case-insensitive substring, or bare --force for all steps. Forcing does not turn a broken step green.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/cli/src/setup.ts#L136-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1442d625a98f55e4134c65b04da72b4d8cc40262ab536b95efb9c8c034cd2fcb:"
        },
